Description: Match operators as Twig 3's Lexer::getOperatorRegex does
 Twig builds one pattern per operator: spaces inside it match any run of
 whitespace, an operator ending in a letter must be followed by whitespace,
 "(", ")", "[" or "{", and an operator starting with a letter is not one
 right after "." or "|", nor after "." or "|" and one whitespace character.
 twig-lexer 1.0.0 had only the lookahead, with "(" alone, and matched on the
 text after the cursor, where a lookbehind sees nothing. The patterns are
 now matched at the cursor against the whole source (sticky flag), so the
 lookbehind is written into the pattern as Twig writes it. Whitespace is
 PCRE's (TL-02), so "a or<NBSP>b" is one name, as in Twig. The comparator
 sorting operators by length is made consistent. The operator list itself
 is not changed here: this package passes Twig's list through the
 protected operators field (src/twig/operators.ts).
Author: Numiko
Origin: other, https://github.com/twigphp/Twig/blob/v3.30.0/src/Lexer.php
Forwarded: not-needed
Twig-Reference: 3.1.0 (lookahead and lookbehind), 3.24.0 (lookbehind with whitespace)
Test: test/fixtures/twig/operators.twig and operator-edges.twig (parity with Twig); npm run test:upstream
Last-Update: 2026-11-03
